# Extracted from the published checkpoint by port/extract_reference.py; regenerate rather
# than commit (weights.npz is 150 MB).
port/reference/
*.npz
__pycache__/

# The authors' TensorFlow checkpoint: 146 MB, two thirds of it Adam's optimizer slots, and
# over GitHub's 100 MB file limit. The weights inference needs are committed as
# port/weights.npz instead. To re-derive them, or to rerun port/verify_port.py against the
# original graph, fetch the checkpoint back:
#     git fetch upstream && git checkout upstream/master -- results/
results/*.data-*
